</div></div></div><div class="fe-block fe-block-6943efb813ed8f2eb56a"><div class="sqs-block website-component-block sqs-block-website-component sqs-block-html html-block sqs-background-enabled" data-block-css="[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.html/fa064889-35e4-452f-a442-609281306ad6_586/website.components.html.styles.css&quot;]" data-block-scripts="[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.html/fa064889-35e4-452f-a442-609281306ad6_586/website.components.html.visitor.js&quot;]" data-block-type="1337" data-definition-name="website.components.html" data-sqsp-block="text" data-website-component-id="6943efb813ed8f2eb56a" id="block-6943efb813ed8f2eb56a"><div class="sqs-block-content"><div class="sqs-text-block-container">
  
  <div class="sqs-html-content" data-sqsp-text-block-content><h4 style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Stephen R. Anderson (1943 - 2025).</h4><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">We are very sad to report that our friend and colleague, Steve Anderson, died on October 13, 2025. In addition to being a member of the Yale Linguistics Department from 1994 until his retirement in 2017, he was a long time member of the Haskins Board of Directors and a supporter of both Haskins and the Endangered Language Fund. He was a brilliant scholar, a friend and mentor to many, and an inspiration. He will be missed.  See the <a href="https://ling.yale.edu/posts/2025-10-14-in-memoriam-stephen-r-anderson">Yale Linguistics In Memoriam page</a> for additional information. </p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">See the <a href="https://www.nytimes.com/2025/11/20/science/stephen-anderson-dead.html" target="">New York Times obituary.</a> </p></div>


  
